{
  "case_id": "2010-09-993",
  "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "EDWIN S. KNEEDLER, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case involves the ordinary operation of the Supremacy Clause. As the government agrees, Hatch-Waxman's plain text requires generic drugs to have the same warnings as their brand-name equivalents, so State law can't require generic drugs to use different warnings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We maintain that a claim that under State law a generic company can be liable for not asking the FDA to make a labeling change is preempted under this Court's decisions both in Buckman and in ArkLa, because what the -- what the Court has said is that the disclosure obligations between a Federal agency and a Federally regulated party are inherently Federal in character, and this is not a subject of traditional State tort law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Lefkowitz",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 27 years of enforcement under Hatch-Waxman, the FDA has never once said that a generic drug that uses the brand label, as required under 505(j) of the statute is misbranded."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Lefkowitz, there's a certain overlap, is there not? Some of the generics are made by the same people that make the brand-name drugs, isn't that so?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, all you're arguing is that this rule will have little practical effect, that there is going to be very few lawsuits that could be brought against your companies because you're just not going to have enough information to suggest a label change."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yeah, but -- but -- no, but -- but surely you have to establish not only that the generic manufacturer requested a label change, but that a label change would have been approved. Otherwise there's no causation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Be sure you answer, please, my original question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just so I understand what you've said, this 3-month turnaround that you mentioned, they are all requests from labeled manufacturers, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0015",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you, and I think that this is part of what your adversary has been talking about when he says we don't usually receive adverse incident reports; they go to the brand manufacturer. So tell me what you view as your main obligation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0018",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose they had. Suppose that -- is a generic required to file adverse incident reports?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0020",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose a generic -- suppose that the FDA issued a rule that says a generic drug manufacturer has no obligation to request a change in labeling. Could a generic drug manufacturer be held liable on a failure to warn claim on the theory that it could have lobbied the FDA to change the rule that says that the generic drug manufacturer has no obligation to ask for a change in labeling?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bograd",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0001-0021",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Their obligation -- their obligation under State law is to provide a warning. What they should have done, and if you take -- what they should have done is go to the FDA and ask the FDA to approve a stronger warning. If the FDA had said no, they would have a preemption."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But your theory is that they have a duty to pursue an informal process that is nowhere provided for under the FDA rules; and so I don't -- so it's a duty to lobby the FDA basically to change the rules, isn't that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there is a formal obligation, both under statute, not to sell a misbranded drug, and under regulation, to revise your labeling as soon as there's reasonable evidence of an association of a serious hazard with the drug."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is your -- what is your explanation for why Buckman isn't applicable here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the suit was not against the manufacturer; the suit in Buckman was against a consultant that -- that helped the manufacturer get FDA approval."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Hatch-Waxman Amendments were designed to facilitate the entry of generic drugs onto the market. They do not absolve a manufacturer of his responsibilities after entry onto the market to maintain the safety of the drug and the adequacy of -- of the label."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Kneedler, suppose that I'm not sure I agree with you that there is an obligation of the kind that you say for a generic drug manufacturer to come forward and request a label, but I do think that there's an opportunity for that manufacturer to come forward and ask the FDA to revise a label. If that's the way I read the law, does your result follow? Do you think, then, that State law claims should be able to go forward?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Has the FDA made any calculation of the economic consequences of imposing this duty on generic drug manufacturers? I don't know whether this is a good idea or not, but it does seem to me that it may significantly increase the costs for generic drug manufacturers, and therefore counteract one of the objectives of the statute, which was to provide generic drugs at a low cost."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Am I -- am I to understand -- and I think I am understanding you. There is a legal obligation in the statute to report adverse events. You're saying that the statute also requires every manufacturer, of whatever type, to monitor the safety of the drug they're selling? Is that what you're saying?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Lefkowitz, do you agree with Justice Ginsburg's characterization of the government's position?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Lefkowitz",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEFKOWITZ: Your Honor, Buckman makes very clear that a State trying to regulate disclosure obligations to the Federal Government is simply off limits, and in fact -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Lefkowitz",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3c4e4102dfa846f72807d51613cabfd0d0e09453270bd23a7dffe46717643f43",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3c4e4102dfa8-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEFKOWITZ: Well, in a sense the government is really saying we -- to lobby or to propose changes is a -- is a very fine distinction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-993",
      "confidence": 0.0,
